# winuxsh residue baseline for scripts/check-rename-clean.sh
# GENERATED — do not edit by hand. Regenerate with:
#     sh scripts/check-rename-clean.sh --regen
# Format: <repo-relative path><TAB><verbatim line text of the hit>
.gitattributes	# Shell scripts are executed by Git Bash / winuxsh, both of which treat CR
AGENTS.md	- Rename brand gate: `sh scripts/check-rename-clean.sh` must pass (residue is an exact baseline diff; runs under Git Bash and `winuxsh -c` alike). Intentional residue change → regenerate `scripts/check-rename-clean.baseline` via `sh scripts/check-rename-clean.sh --regen` and review the diff.
AGENTS.md	- Runtime environment variables use the `NATIVE_SHELL_` prefix. During the transition, native-shell also sets/reads the deprecated `WINUXSH_SHELL` and `WINUXSH_ROOT` names because current rubash upstream still reads them; these bridges are marked with comments and must be removed once rubash renames its readers. (The `*_SHELL_PATH_STYLE` pair was retired rubash-side in rubash#556 / rubash#537: the engine always renders `$PWD`/`pwd` in the POSIX persona form, and native-shell no longer exports the variables.)
AGENTS.md	- Use `~/.native-shellrc` as the primary-only interactive user entry point for plugin lists, theme selection, exports, aliases, functions, and shell startup logic. Do not read, migrate, delete, or modify the legacy `~/.winuxshrc` and `~/.winshrc` startup files. An explicitly opted-in `~/.bashrc` fallback is a future plan only, not supported behavior. Startup must not automatically run setup or plugin sync, create the primary rc, or rewrite user rc files. Issue #359 case A (1.4.2): plugin management never writes the rc at all — the manifest (`plugins.toml` + `sources/registry.toml`) drives the generated loader `~/.native-shell/generated/plugins.nsh`, which the host sources read-only BEFORE the user rc; `native-shell setup` still writes the rc (create/whole-file) until its 1.4.3 create-only convergence. Never re-attach the retired managed-block writers (`assets::write_managed_block`/`remove_managed_block`) to any verb — the 359.12 structure ratchet fails the build's test suite if you do.
CHANGELOG.md	  (`${NIU_SHELL:-niu}`), so a stale native-shell on PATH can no longer hijack it;
CHANGELOG.md	  POSIX mode and the `NIU_SHELL` contract verified through the links.
CHANGELOG.md	  `NIU_INVOKED_AS` forward now carries all four faces
CHANGELOG.md	  cleared of `*.bak-*` / `*.old-*` / `*.niu-old-*` on install and uninstall —
CHANGELOG.md	  forwards its argv[0] stem as `NIU_INVOKED_AS` (actively scrubbed
CHANGELOG.md	  machines; `*.niu-old-*` covers a relinker crash between park and drop).
CHANGELOG.md	  niu-git moves to `layout: flat`: the payload lands under `opt\native-git` and
CHANGELOG.md	  niu-git question prints the same cancelled note as every other question;
CHANGELOG.md	  niu-vs-cmd-vs-powershell decision guidance) and installs it into agent
CHANGELOG.md	- **Windows releases bundle niu-git 2.55.0.5** (`scripts/release/preinstall.json`).
CHANGELOG.md	- `argv[0]`-marked login shells (`-bash`, `-niu`) preserve `shopt login_shell` as `on` across `reset_shell_options` (#465, rubash#911).
