scripts/release/preinstall.json	      "purpose": "Niu-git 2.56.0.1 (native Windows git without MSYS; real git-for-windows C source built with MSVC, no POSIX layer). The full plugin distro (oh-my-bash, omb-theme-robbyrussell, bash-it, bash-completion, bash-preexec) installs every entry through git clone/pull, so a fresh machine without git.exe on PATH failed all five with 'failed to run git; is git.exe on PATH?' (native-shell#209). Bundling native-git removes the hard dependency on the user's environment. 2.56.0.1 is layout=flat: the payload lands under <root>\\opt\\native-git (mingw64/ + etc/) and mingw64/bin/git.exe is mapped straight onto usr\\bin\\git.exe, so the git on PATH IS the git binary - no launcher, no winuxcmd dispatch hop, and git --version drops from 72-83 ms to ~14 ms (Git Bash: 45-103 ms). Requires WinuxCmd 1.1.9 or newer in the same release (wpm#1183: POSIX-unlink hardlink break, without which the flat mapping cannot replace the usr\\bin hardlink). It is schannel-only TLS with no bundled shell/perl (shell-script parts of git run on native-shell's sh) and accepts POSIX-shaped (/d/...) path args.",
scripts/release/rubash-pin.json	    "Pinned to JayWanX/rubash 0c955b4a - 'Send the invocation face under the current variable name'. The shim forwarded the bash/sh invocation face as NIU_INVOKED_AS while Native Shell reads NATIVE_SHELL_INVOKED_AS, so `bash --help` printed the product help and failed the staged-release face gate, and `bash -c 'echo $0'` printed native-shell instead of bash.",
scripts/release/rubash-pin.json	    "The same fork carries e84ffd77 - 'Find the host shell by its current name, not the pre-rename one' - which rewires the shim's locate_shell() from niu.exe/winuxsh.exe to native-shell.exe. Without both commits a staged <root>/cmd/usr/bin/bash.exe neither finds the shell (exit 127) nor reproduces the GNU face.",
scripts/release/rubash-pin.json	  "description": "Rubash source pin for native-shell releases (rubash#827, conclusion B). Every release job fetches exactly this rubash commit into ../rubash -- where the [patch] path override in Cargo.toml deterministically picks it up -- and fails the release unless the checked-out HEAD equals rubash_rev. The compiled engine is pinned to an exact commit instead of being 'whatever rubash master HEAD was at build time'. The engine now comes from JayWanX/rubash (our fork): upstream unixwin/rubash still ships the pre-rename bash shim lookup chain (niu.exe / winuxsh.exe), which cannot find native-shell.exe and exits 127.",
scripts/run-realworld-with-native-shell.sh	    run_niu "eval \"\$(cat '$tmp')\"$extra; echo eval-ok"
